            (b)         a contractual obligation that is conditional on a counterparty exercising its right to redeem is a
                        financial liability because the entity does not have the unconditional right to avoid delivering cash
                        or another financial asset.
20          A financial instrument that does not explicitly establish a contractual obligation to deliver cash or another
            financial asset may establish an obligation indirectly through its terms and conditions. For example:
            (a)         a financial instrument may contain a non-financial obligation that must be settled if, and only if,
                        the entity fails to make distributions or to redeem the instrument. If the entity can avoid a transfer
